From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <barak+git@pearlmutter.net>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:32:38 +0100
Subject: compare: fingerprint pages once, and keep them between comparisons

Comparing a pair of pages needs only a few facts about each page: its
words and their positions and, in Appearance mode, its 72 DPI
rendering.  comparePagesInParallel() now computes these per page, as a
PageFingerprint with the rendering kept as a hash, rather than per pair,
and compares pairs by their fingerprints (compareFingerprints()), so:

- a page that occurs in several pairs is processed once;
- the GUI keeps the fingerprints (MainWindow::fingerprints), keyed by
  file path, size and modification time, page, and margins, so comparing
  again takes milliseconds: on a 140-page pair, Words mode took 186 ms
  the first time and 10 ms the second in DiffPDF, where this comes from;
  switching to Appearance adds only the rendering hashes;
- any page can be paired with any other without asking Poppler again,
  which the page offset (next commit) needs.

The fingerprinting workers keep the cap on their number
(PageCompareOptions::maxWorkers, the CompareThreads setting) and the
wait for every one of them even when one throws, from 1cbb8c4.

Fingerprints of files no longer being compared are dropped.  Batch mode
passes no cache.  The progress callback now reports pages fingerprinted
out of pages to do.  disparPDFc gives the same results and --pdfdiff
page counts as before on 72 comparisons (8 file pairs, 3 modes, 3
margin/zoom settings).

